# Review of the merged reports

The original incident page says one parser issue explains all reports. The desk's cause view
also identifies a different problem: the booking-v3 date hint tells day-first tenants to enter
month first, while that form reads the date in the tenant's order.

The table below groups unique reports by the desk's current tenant and channel rules. Intake
labels are guesses, not a cause. The rule does not inspect report text, so its groups are a
starting point for investigation, not proof that every report has the assigned cause.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table describes the exported desk queue, not the new GitHub issues. We filed
[the parser issue](https://github.com/aleakos/scratch/issues/1) and
[the booking-v3 hint issue](https://github.com/aleakos/scratch/issues/2) separately.

## One-day shifts need review

Five reports in the desk notes describe a one-day move or otherwise suggest it. They remain
in their rule-assigned group in the table. Check their booking times, time zones, and invite
conversion before assigning a cause; the reports alone do not prove a shared time-zone bug.

## Why the merge needs review

The accepted deduplication decision matches subjects rather than report content. Similar
subjects can therefore hide different problems. Review the cause and evidence before merging;
do not treat the subject as proof of a duplicate.

## Queue history

The desk continued merging reports after they arrived. The timeline compares receipt and
merge dates; it is built from the export when this page renders.

